---
id: spiced-butter-glazed-wild-pollock
title: Butter-Glazed Pollock
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 240

storage:
  fridge_days: 3
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Submerge the sealed pouches of @wild-pollock-fillet{400%g} in a bowl of cold tap water for ~thaw-time{10%min} until completely pliable.

Remove fillets from packaging and sandwich them between 4 layers of paper towels. Press down firmly with both hands to squeeze out excess processing moisture (crucial to prevent fillets from boiling into watery mush).

Set the #oven to convection 200°C (400°F) and let it preheat fully, about 10 to 15 minutes. Lay the pressed fillets on the mesh basket of the #crisper-tray, so any liquid they still release drips away instead of pooling. Brush tops evenly with melted @unsalted-butter{1/2%tbsp}, then dust with @smoked-paprika{1/2%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1/2%tsp}, @onion-powder{1/2%tsp}, @black-pepper{1/4%tsp}, and @dried-dill{1/4%tsp}. (Do not add salt; the brined fillets naturally provide full seasoning).

Bake on the middle rack for ~bake-time{10%min}, checking from the 8-minute mark, until opaque and flaking easily at the thickest point.

Immediately squeeze juice from @fresh-lemon{1/2} over the hot fillets, and transfer the single cooked portion (240 g cooked yield) into a meal prep container.
